- Runway based on net burn (cash outflow net of revenue) — common for fast-growing companies reporting “months until cash runs out given current net burn.”
- Runway based on gross burn (total cash outflow, ignoring incoming revenue) — less common but sometimes used for conservative runway.
- Runway that includes planned/forecasted step-up in expenses (e.g., hiring, capex) or one-time outflows — i.e., runway computed from a projected monthly deficit that’s different from current trailing‑12/trailing‑3 net burn.
